-- title:
--   The standard Grassmannian chart is represented by Sym_R(M^k)/J
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring, $M$ an $R$-module, $k$ a natural number and $x : \mathrm{Fin}\,k \to M$ a $k$-tuple of elements of $M$. For a commutative $R$-algebra $A$ write $U_x(A)$ for the subtype of `Module.Grassmannian A (A ⊗[R] M) k` — submodules $N \subseteq A \otimes_R M$ whose quotient is finitely generated projective of rank $k$ — consisting of those $N$ for which the map $A^{k} \to (A \otimes_R M)/N$, $v \mapsto \sum_i v_i \cdot \overline{1 \otimes x_i}$, is bijective. The theorem asserts the existence of an ideal $J$ of the symmetric algebra $\mathrm{Sym}_R(\mathrm{Fin}\,k \to M)$ together with a proof that $J$ is the ideal generated by the elements $\iota(\mathrm{Pi.single}\,i\,(x_j)) - \delta_{ij}$ for $i, j \in \mathrm{Fin}\,k$, where $\iota$ is the canonical map of the symmetric algebra and $\mathrm{Pi.single}\,i\,m$ is the tuple with $m$ in slot $i$ and $0$ elsewhere, and of a family of bijections $\mathrm{pt}_A : U_x(A) \simeq (\mathrm{Sym}_R(\mathrm{Fin}\,k \to M)/J \to_{\mathrm{alg}[R]} A)$, one for each commutative $R$-algebra $A$, such that: (i) for every such $A$, every $N \in U_x(A)$ and every $m \in M$ one has $\sum_i \mathrm{pt}_A(N)(\overline{\iota(\mathrm{Pi.single}\,i\,m)}) \cdot \overline{1 \otimes x_i} = \overline{1 \otimes m}$ in $(A \otimes_R M)/N$, i.e. the images under $\mathrm{pt}_A(N)$ of the classes of $\iota(\mathrm{Pi.single}\,i\,m)$ are the coordinates of $\overline{1 \otimes m}$ in the basis $(\overline{1 \otimes x_i})_i$; and (ii) for every $R$-algebra map $\varphi : A \to B$ and every $N \in U_x(A)$, the base change `Module.Grassmannian.map φ N` again satisfies the bijectivity condition, and with that witness $\mathrm{pt}_B$ of the base change equals $\mathrm{pt}_A(N)$ followed by $\varphi$.
--
--   This is the affine representability of a standard chart of the Grassmannian functor of an arbitrary module: the chart at a $k$-tuple $x$ is the functor of points of $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\mathrm{Sym}_R(M^{\oplus k})$ modulo the $k^2$ linear relations sending $x_j$ to the $j$-th standard idempotent coordinate. It supplies the affine members of the open cover used in [`Module.Grassmannian.exists_scheme_represents_and_isAffineOpen_chart_cover`](thm.html#Module.Grassmannian.exists_scheme_represents_and_isAffineOpen_chart_cover), where the Grassmannian is glued as a scheme.
